    "text": "To determine the total number of tabs James opened, we need to break down the problem step by step.\n\n1. Identify the number of browsers James has. He has 2 browsers.\n2. Determine the number of windows in each browser. Each browser has 3 windows.\n3. Determine the number of tabs in each window. Each window has 10 tabs.\n4. Calculate the total number of tabs in one browser. Since each browser has 3 windows and each window has 10 tabs, the total number of tabs in one browser is:\n   \\[\n   3 \\text{ windows} \\times 10 \\text{ tabs per window} = 30 \\text{ tabs}\n   \\]\n5. Since James has 2 browsers, the total number of tabs in both browsers is:\n   \\[\n   2 \\text{ browsers} \\times 30 \\text{ tabs per browser} = 60 \\text{ tabs}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of tabs James opened in all the browsers together is \\(\\boxed{60}\\).",
